            "review_text": "OzTravellerBrisbane\nBrisbane188 contributions\n0\nPlenty to satisfy anyone\nNov 2014 • Solo\nThe restaurant chain is best described as hotpot meets sushi train. A conveyor belt selection of different food to cook in a soup of spicy or non-spicy.\n\nThe hotpot variety is of good quality, and for anyone not liking this, there is a small selection of sushi and fried Japanese selections. The standard lunch price is around USD $8 for all you can eat. Perhaps the only criticism is the lack of a good range of Japanese desserts.\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten December 2, 2014",
